message.content:
Sure! If you want to look up what address (or other place information) corresponds to the latitude 37.4224764 and longitude ‑122.0842499, you would use the **reverse‑geocoding** endpoint of the Google Maps Geocoding API.

Below is an example of how you would make the request and what a typical JSON response looks like. (If you run this yourself you’ll see the exact details for that location.)

---

### 1️⃣ Build the request URL

```text
https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY
```

* `latlng` – the latitude and longitude you’re querying, separated by a comma.
* `key` – your personal Google Maps API key.

> **Tip:** If you don’t have a key yet, you can create one in the Google Cloud Console under “APIs & Services → Credentials”.

---

### 2️⃣ Example response (JSON)

```json
{
   "results" : [
      {
         "address_components" : [
            {
               "long_name" : "1600",
               "short_name" : "1600",
               "types" : [ "street_number" ]
            },
            {
               "long_name" : "Amphitheatre Parkway",
               "short_name" : "Amphitheatre Pkwy",
               "types" : [ "route" ]
            },
            {
               "long_name" : "Mountain View",
               "short_name" : "Mountain View",
               "types" : [ "locality", "political" ]
            },
            {
               "long_name" : "Santa Clara County",
               "short_name" : "Santa Clara County",
               "types" : [ "administrative_area_level_2", "political" ]
            },
            {
               "long_name" : "California",
               "short_name" : "CA",
               "types" : [ "administrative_area_level_1", "political" ]
            },
            {
               "long_name" : "United States",
               "short_name" : "US",
               "types" : [ "country", "political" ]
            }
         ],
         "formatted_address" : "1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA",
         "geometry" : {
            "location" : {
               "lat" : 37.4224764,
               "lng" : -122.0842499
            },
            "location_type" : "ROOFTOP",
            "viewport" : {
               "northeast" : {
                  "lat" : 37.4238253802915,
                  "lng" : -122.0829009197085
               },
               "southwest" : {
                  "lat" : 37.4211274197085,
                  "lng" : -122.0855988802915
               }
            }
         },
         "place_id" : "ChIJj61dQgK6j4ARw7e8ZcYfXxE",
         "plus_code" : {
            "compound_code" : "CWC8+WQ Mountain View, CA, USA",
            "global_code" : "849VCWC8+WQ"
         },
         "types" : [ "street_address" ]
      }
   ],
   "status" : "OK"
}
```

> **What you’ll see:**  
> * `formatted_address` gives the full street address.  
> * `geometry.location` confirms the same latitude/longitude you queried.  
> * `place_id` is a unique identifier for that location.  
> * `plus_code` is a short, human‑readable location code.

---

### 3️⃣ How to parse the response in JavaScript

```js
fetch('https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY')
  .then(r => r.json())
  .then(data => {
    if (data.status === 'OK') {
      const result = data.results[0];
      console.log('Address:', result.formatted_address);
      console.log('Place ID:', result.place_id);
    } else {
      console.error('Geocoding error:', data.status);
    }
  })
  .catch(err => console.error('Network error:', err));
```

---

### 4️⃣ What you’ll get back

Running the above request will return the address for the Googleplex (the headquarters of Google). The coordinates you supplied are indeed the canonical “Googleplex” location:

```
Latitude: 37.4224764
Longitude: -122.0842499
Formatted Address: 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA
```

Feel free to replace the latitude/longitude values with any other coordinates you’re interested in, and the API will give you the corresponding address (or other place details) in the same format.
